[1mHello, Forme

[0mThis is the inaugural post of the [1mCoding Adventures blog[0m, and the first piece of content shipped end-to-end through the [4mForme <https://github.com/adhithyan15/coding-adventures>[0m universal authoring pipeline.

The path it took from data/2026-05-15-hello-forme.md to /coding-adventures/blog/2026-05-15-hello-forme.html is exactly the shape laid out in the FM00 spec:

The complete pipeline is listed below. With JavaScript enabled, optional controls can focus one step at a time.

1. [1mforme-source-fs[0m walked data/, found this file, and emitted a ContentSource.
2. [1mforme-parse-markdown[0m split off the frontmatter you see above, parsed the body as GFM, and emitted a ContentNode.
3. [1mblog-attach-interactivity[0m attached the one reviewed pipeline-step module to this post and left every other post without a script asset.
4. [1mforme-resolve-asset-refs-fs[0m discovered the local diagram below, assigned its stable logical identity, and preserved its fragment target.
5. [1mforme-router[0m assigned one canonical route, then fanned the routed node out to the page and collection branches.
6. [1mforme-collect-chronological[0m sorted this and the other posts by date while preserving that canonical route.
7. [1mforme-render-static[0m matched the reusable classless Style IR theme, recorded usedStyle, compiled the page slice through the AOT path, and emitted a RenderedPage with exact island usage and asset placeholders.
8. [1mforme-render-terminal[0m compiled the same routed content and classless Style IR theme to safe ANSI text, preserved fallback content, and recorded every unsupported style, asset, raw node, and island as explicit data.
9. [1mforme-render-terminal/package[0m assembled those terminal buffers into a deterministic capability-free artifact with .ansi and degradation files.
10. [1mforme-load-assets-fs[0m loaded and hashed the SVG and JavaScript bytes while enforcing canonical storage-root containment.
11. [1mblog-surface[0m rendered the chronological collection into the blog index, RSS, Atom, and sitemap artifacts.
12. [1mforme-emit-site-fs[0m joined the rendered page and asset streams, replaced placeholders with fingerprinted public URLs, emitted only the selected script, and recorded the article DeployArtifact manifest.
13. [1mforme-emit-fs[0m wrote the index, feeds, and sitemap through the independent surface branch.

[image: Forme turns source content into reusable IR and many output surfaces.]

The point isn't the post — it's that everything between the parser and the deployer is [3mplug-compatible[0m. Want a different theme? Pass a different resolved StyleDocument; the renderer does not change. Want to ship to S3 instead of disk? Replace forme-emit-site-fs. The rest of the DAG stays put.

> One pipeline, many surfaces. That's the Forme bet.

The next few posts will work through what the kernel + orchestrator gives you, and how collection outputs grow into indexes and feeds.
